{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## NOW UNBLOCKED — J1 `acb2` closed (Gerrit change 1009 merged, `gerrit/main` @ `7fc96b277`)\n\nThis story is next in the queue and `review-plan` will no longer fast-fail. Start with:\n\n```sh\ncd /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family    # branch jira-family-seam, @ 7fc96b277 == gerrit/main\nenv PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" rebar review-plan 62d9-9f6d-ecf4-4743   # ~18-22 min\n```\n\n**Record J1's Gerrit change number (1009) on this ticket before pushing** — that is the epic's *'oracles written before any code moved'* proof (epic AC8). J1's oracles are merged and must pass **unmodified** across this change; if one of them fails, the extraction changed behavior.\n\nJ1 delivered 30 pinned tests in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_characterization.py`, with proven teeth (three mutations each turned it RED). Treat them as the held-out oracle, not a spec to code against.\n\nRead this ticket's **previous comment** first — it lists the three defects fixed in this story's plan, including the two that will bite an implementer: **absolute imports only** into the location-pinned modules, and the **`deleted -> Done`** decision being a deliberate declared behavior change rather than a pure move."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785338700245680001,"uuid":"fcfd5aa5-28e9-4490-ac89-5d42c2cc55f2"}